# The disk calls (tests/programs/storage.asm): known sectors of every drive
# read, a marked sector written to each and read back (and found on the
# host's images afterwards), arguments refused, registers kept.
program: storage
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs mame
sector: A 2000 rx286 wrote this to A: sector 2000
sector: B 700 rx286 wrote this to B: sector 700
sector: C 41819 rx286 wrote this to C: sector 41819
sector: D 20000 rx286 wrote this to D: sector 20000
---
rx286, test build
A: sector 0: label 'RX286      ', signature AA55
B: sector 0: label 'RX286B     ', signature AA55
B: the motor's start: the ticks went on
C: sector 0: partition type 01 from sector 17, signature AA55
C: sector 17: label 'RX286C     ', signature AA55
D: sector 0: partition type 01 from sector 17, signature AA55
D: sector 17: label 'RX286D     ', signature AA55
A: the last sector: read
B: the last sector: read
C: the last sector: read
D: the last sector: read
A: sector 2000: written and read back
B: sector 700: written and read back
C: sector 41819: written and read back
D: sector 20000: written and read back
read: drive 4: error 3
read: A's sector 2400: error 3
read: into CS: error 1
read: across the data's limit: error 1
read: through a null ES: error 1
write: from a null DS: error 1
write: C's sector 41820: error 3
read: registers kept
